      ></video>
      <div class="card-caption">
        <strong>Motion-model with preprocessed mesh data.</strong> The geodesic distances for all face pairs are computed offline and stored in
        ascending order. Using this data structure, the random walk is applied simply by changing the face index of a particle (about 0.06 µs to
        update one particle).
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h3 class="project-subsection-title">3. Measurement-model</h3>
  <p>
    A smaller QP error implies that the particle well-explains the sensor measurements, so the weight of a particle is defined using the QP error,
    $w^{[m]}_i \propto \exp\!\big(-\alpha\,\mathrm{QP}(\hat{\mathbf{W}} \mid \mathbf{x}^{[m]}_i, \mathbf{x}^{*})\big)$. In the multi-contact case,
    instead of evaluating all possible pairs of particles, particles $\mathbf{x}^{*}$ are sampled from the other particle sets considering the
    associated weights.
  </p>
  <h3 class="project-subsection-title">4. Exploration particles</h3>
  <div class="project-grid project-grid-2">
    <div class="project-media-card">
      <a
        aria-label="Open full image: Distance between faces in different links"
        href="{{ '/assets/img/research/mcpep/geodesic_distance.webp' | relative_url }}"
        ><img
          alt="Distance between faces in different links"
          decoding="async"
          loading="lazy"
          src="{{ '/assets/img/research/mcpep/geodesic_distance.webp' | relative_url }}"
      ></a>
      <div class="card-caption">
        While the distance between faces in the same link is constant, the distance between faces in different links changes as the joint rotates, so
        it cannot be precomputed. Consequently, the motion model changes face#, but not link#.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="project-media-card">
      <video
        aria-label="Exploration particles (yellow) are forced to investigate adjacent links. If the maximum weight of a particle set is lower than a threshold, one particle is randomly discarded from the basic set (pink), and a new particle with an adjacent link# is added to the explore set. Exploration particles do not undergo resampling, so basic particles can be resampled around them on the correct link."
        controls=""
        loop=""
        muted=""
        playsinline=""
        poster="{{ '/assets/video/research/mcpep/mcpep_exploration.jpg' | relative_url }}"
        preload="none"
        src="{{ '/assets/video/research/mcpep/mcpep_exploration.mp4' | relative_url }}"
      ></video>
      <div class="card-caption">
        <strong>Exploration particles (yellow)</strong> are forced to investigate adjacent links. If the maximum weight of a particle set is lower
        than a threshold, one particle is randomly discarded from the basic set (pink), and a new particle with an adjacent link# is added to the
        explore set. Exploration particles do not undergo resampling, so basic particles can be resampled around them on the correct link.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
