  <h2 class="project-section-title">Results</h2>
  <h3 class="project-subsection-title">Simulation validation</h3>
  <p>
    The algorithm is implemented in the MuJoCo simulator with a 7-DOF Franka Emika Panda robot arm equipped with JTSs, and tested as a single-thread
    C++ program. Single, dual, and triple contact scenarios are simulated 10000 times each. At each run, the robot configuration was initialized
    randomly, and a 20 N force in the friction cone was applied at a random position (up to 1 contact per link). A case with ≤ 2.25 cm localization
    error (roughly 5 faces) is classified as a success.
  </p>
